{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYoi79iZZ2q4TMDzQGh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenAI's announcement that it will honor a common robots.txt signal is narrower than it may first sound. The signal concerns one use of website content, the training of foundational generative AI models. The article does not describe it as covering any other use of a site's pages, so operators should not assume it extends further than that.\n\nWithin that scope, the change is about consolidation. Website operators who wanted to express a training preference previously had to identify individual crawlers and keep separate rules for every provider. A shared signal lets them communicate one preference to multiple participating providers at once. OpenAI says it is joining other participants in the IETF's AI Preferences working group in announcing the signal, which means the definition comes from a standards discussion that is still ongoing and not from a single company's format.\n\nSeveral things remain open. OpenAI says it aims to implement the signal in the coming months and will publish another update with implementation details. It calls the effort voluntary and encourages other AI providers to honor the signal, without naming who else has committed to do so. It also says the signal will not replace its existing robots.txt crawler controls, which will continue to apply and be respected, so operators will for now be working with both mechanisms.\n\nOpenAI describes the move as a practical step toward an open web where website owners have clearer, simpler ways to communicate how their content is used. Whether it achieves that depends on the implementation details still to come and on how many other providers follow."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_read_input_tokens":3504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c899ed8e-5f38-49f9-949d-389955c32d7d","uuid":"2babf294-a484-408e-9054-24aa5a99b52f","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:28:26.331Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYohuk42SmqYvnwsHEB"}
